1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,617
In Indonesia, a small fault on a motorbike or a water pump can cost a day's wage.

2
00:00:07,617 --> 00:00:12,820
Repair videos can't see your problem, and most of them aren't in your language.

3
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:15,179
Take a photo and say what's wrong.

4
00:00:15,179 --> 00:00:19,904
This run is in demo mode, with AI-generated sample photos.

5
00:00:19,904 --> 00:00:24,691
Each stage shows its result as soon as it finishes: what Muse Spark saw,

6
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:28,716
the parts SAM 3.1 outlined, then the likely cause.

7
00:00:28,716 --> 00:00:34,336
When the evidence is ambiguous, it asks one short question instead of guessing.

8
00:00:34,336 --> 00:00:37,617
Then the diagnosis: likely causes with confidence,

9
00:00:37,617 --> 00:00:43,436
a safety level, tools, time, and the parts cost next to the repair-shop price.

10
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:49,872
SAM 3.1 masks and numbers the parts on your own photo, not on a generic diagram.

11
00:00:49,872 --> 00:00:52,728
Before step one there's a short safety checklist.

12
00:00:52,728 --> 00:00:56,284
The steps stay locked until every item is ticked.

13
00:00:56,284 --> 00:01:02,340
The live camera guide: point the phone and SAM 3.1 outlines the part to touch, about once a second.

14
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:07,016
Here the camera is Chromium's fake camera playing a sample photo.

15
00:01:07,016 --> 00:01:08,832
After each step, Check my step.

16
00:01:08,832 --> 00:01:11,995
Muse Spark compares the photo with the expected state.

17
00:01:11,995 --> 00:01:16,620
This one is too dark, so it asks for the torch instead of guessing.

18
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:20,620
Retake it, and the step is verified before you move on.

19
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:21,442
Hands dirty?

20
00:01:21,442 --> 00:01:22,744
Turn on hands-free.

21
00:01:22,744 --> 00:01:28,376
Each step is read aloud, and the phone listens for lanjut, ulang or cek.

22
00:01:28,376 --> 00:01:29,321
Still broken?

23
00:01:29,321 --> 00:01:34,045
Say what happened, and it re-plans to the next most likely cause.

24
00:01:34,045 --> 00:01:36,708
Plan, act, verify, re-plan.

25
00:01:36,708 --> 00:01:41,892
When a photo can't show a step, Muse Image draws a diagram and Muse Spark checks it.

26
00:01:41,892 --> 00:01:45,184
In demo mode the drawing is a placeholder.

27
00:01:45,184 --> 00:01:53,852
Every decision is on screen: what it saw, why it asked, each photo check, each re-plan, and which Meta model did it.

28
00:01:53,852 --> 00:01:59,421
When it's a job for a pro, one tap hands it off: a WhatsApp summary of what was found and tried,

29
00:01:59,421 --> 00:02:04,008
a search for the nearest bengkel, and a PDF brief for the mechanic.

30
00:02:04,008 --> 00:02:05,823
It also knows when to say no.

31
00:02:05,823 --> 00:02:13,156
Fixing a rice cooker that won't heat means opening 220 volt internals, so the safety gate stops the guide.

32
00:02:13,156 --> 00:02:15,579
It works in WhatsApp too, in Javanese.

33
00:02:15,579 --> 00:02:22,212
Send a photo and the same agent replies with the marked photo, the diagnosis and a button for each step.

34
00:02:22,212 --> 00:02:25,016
A gas leak still gets a red stop.

35
00:02:25,016 --> 00:02:31,502
With one switch, diagnosis and planning run on Muse Spark Open, Meta's open-weights model, on Baseten.

36
00:02:31,502 --> 00:02:34,428
The app shows a badge when it does.

37
00:02:34,428 --> 00:02:38,078
Under the hood: Voice Transcribe, Muse Spark to see,

38
00:02:38,078 --> 00:02:43,905
reason and check, SAM 3.1 for masks and live tracking, and Muse Image for diagrams.

39
00:02:43,905 --> 00:02:47,272
The safety rules are enforced in code.

40
00:02:47,272 --> 00:02:48,236
Tukang Copilot.

41
00:02:48,236 --> 00:02:53,472
Every phone becomes a mechanic's apprentice.
